WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.666 --> 00:00:34.833


2
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:37.416
<b> In this first verse of the Gita,</b>

3
00:00:37.416 --> 00:00:40.333
<b>Dhritarashtra asks Sanjaya,</b>

4
00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:41.875
<b>O Sanjaya, </b>

5
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.916
<b>In the holy land of Kurukshetra,</b>

6
00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:50.541
<b>what did my sons and the sons of Pandu do</b>
<b>when they assembled for battle?</b>

7
00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:56.666
<b>Now we will understand the context of</b>
<b>when and why this was said,</b>

8
00:00:56.666 --> 00:01:05.208
<b>and even more importantly, what life lessons</b>
<b>we can learn from the teachings of the Gita.</b>

9
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:10.041


10
00:01:10.041 --> 00:01:13.458
<b> The battle of Mahabharata is about to begin.</b>

11
00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:17.083
<b>Both armies are positioned face to face.</b>

12
00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:21.916
<b> On one side are the Pandavas,</b>
<b>who stand for truth and dharma,</b>

13
00:01:21.916 --> 00:01:23.458
<b>On the other side are</b>

14
00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.791
<b>the sons of Dhritarashtra, the Kauravas,</b>

15
00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:34.625
<b>who resorted to every path of deceit, trickery,</b>
<b>and adharma to maintain their rule</b>

16
00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:38.333
<b>In such a situation, this battle is not just between</b>
<b>the Pandavas and Kauravas,</b>

17
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.666
<b>but also between dharma and adharma.</b>

18
00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:43.541
<b> And it is being fought at Kurukshetra, </b>

19
00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:49.500
<b>which is a highly revered, sacred place</b>
<b>for the Kuru dynasty.</b>

20
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:55.000
<b>The fact that his sons are siding with adharma</b>
<b>on such holy land ...</b>

21
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.333
<b>is deeply unsettling for Dhritarashtra. </b>

22
00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:06.875
<b>He knows that truth, dharma, and Lord Krishna</b>
<b>are with the Pandavas.</b>

23
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:10.333
<b>But what can be done about the greed </b>

24
00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:14.208
<b>in his mind that says the</b>
<b>Kauravas should win this war</b>

25
00:02:14.208 --> 00:02:19.625
<b>and the rule of Dhritarashtra and</b>
<b>his son Duryodhana should forever remain.</b>

26
00:02:19.625 --> 00:02:22.333
<b>Dhritarashtra could not see with his eyes.</b>

27
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:23.000
<b> But </b>

28
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:30.125
<b>attachment to his sons and greed for</b>
<b>the kingdom had blinded his mind years ago.</b>

29
00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:31.125
<b>Every time</b>

30
00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:36.625
<b> he avoided showing his sons</b>

31
00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:37.250
<b>today</b>

32
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.208
<b>the lives of those very sons are at stake.</b>

33
00:02:41.208 --> 00:02:42.333
<b> Alas!</b>

34
00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:44.750
<b>There's no turning back now.</b>

35
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:45.916
<b>O Sanjaya,</b>

36
00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:53.291
<b>what did my sons and the sons of Pandu do</b>
<b>when they assembled for battle?</b>

37
00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:59.041
<b>When there's deceit in the mind, it's only</b>
<b>natural for worry to reflect in the voice.</b>

38
00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:03.833


39
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:06.750
<b>Everyone has desires.</b>

40
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.750
<b>Dhritarashtra had them too. </b>

41
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.416
<b>So is having desires wrong? </b>

42
00:03:12.416 --> 00:03:13.958
<b>Absolutely not!</b>

43
00:03:13.958 --> 00:03:17.208
<b>Desires are a part of being human; </b>

44
00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:19.875
<b>they are not wrong in themselves.</b>

45
00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:26.166
<b>What's wrong is becoming blinded</b>
<b>by greed in their pursuit</b>

46
00:03:26.166 --> 00:03:31.625
<b> and knowingly straying from the right path.</b>

47
00:03:31.625 --> 00:03:33.416
<b>When this happens,</b>

48
00:03:33.416 --> 00:03:39.833
<b>we become a home to all those</b>
<b>habits that push us back.</b>

49
00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:48.541
<b>And all the habits necessary for</b>
<b>progress become weakened.</b>

50
00:03:48.541 --> 00:03:54.416
<b>Perhaps Dhritarashtra's attachment to</b>
<b>his sons was not wrong;</b>

51
00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:55.833
<b>it was natural.</b>

52
00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:57.458
<b>What was wrong</b>

53
00:03:57.458 --> 00:04:01.041
<b>was closing his eyes in that attachment,</b>

54
00:04:01.041 --> 00:04:11.250
<b>never giving proper guidance on his sons' minor</b>
<b>or major mistakes out of love and affection.  </b>

55
00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:16.583
<b>But can't you make such mistakes too?</b>

56
00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:18.458
<b>Absolutely. </b>

57
00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:21.208
<b> It's natural.</b>

58
00:04:21.208 --> 00:04:27.291
<b>But when mistakes are repeated knowingly,</b>

59
00:04:27.291 --> 00:04:31.166
<b> they become not mistakes but character.</b>

60
00:04:31.166 --> 00:04:40.583
<b>And such fragmented character</b>
<b>shapes or spoils our future.</b>

61
00:04:40.583 --> 00:04:42.958
<b>The war of Mahabharata,</b>

62
00:04:42.958 --> 00:04:48.000
<b>in which all of Dhritarashtra's</b>
<b>sons were sacrificed,</b>

63
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.125
<b>did not happen suddenly one day.</b>

64
00:04:51.125 --> 00:05:01.208
<b>It was the result of repeating</b>
<b>many small mistakes and greeds.</b>

65
00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:02.708
<b>Good or bad,</b>

66
00:05:02.708 --> 00:05:06.625
<b>the destination never comes unexpectedly –</b>

67
00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:11.291
<b>every journey is made up of many small steps.</b>

68
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:16.375
<b>And it is necessary to take these</b>
<b>steps in accordance with dharma</b>

69
00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:20.125
<b>Our mind is also a holy land,</b>

70
00:05:20.125 --> 00:05:22.750
<b>a small Kurukshetra,</b>

71
00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:33.666
<b> where such small battles of Mahabharata between right</b>
<b>and wrong decisions keep happening every day. </b>

72
00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:37.750
<b>And each such inner battle is an opportunity</b>

73
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.666
<b>to choose</b>

74
00:05:39.666 --> 00:05:44.000
<b>whether we will support the</b>
<b>right or the wrong today.</b>

75
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.041
<b>Making the right decision</b>
<b>at the right time is necessary,</b>

76
00:05:48.041 --> 00:05:53.083
<b>and our conscience knows</b>
<b>well what is right and wrong.</b>

77
00:05:53.083 --> 00:05:57.541
<b>What is needed is just to follow it.</b>

78
00:05:57.541 --> 00:06:01.750
<b> And these small battles will determine </b>

79
00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.458
<b>our future.</b>

80
00:06:04.458 --> 00:06:06.541
<b>We have to think</b>

81
00:06:06.541 --> 00:06:10.666
<b>about what habits we will house</b>
<b>within ourselves.</b>

82
00:06:10.666 --> 00:06:11.625
<b>Those</b>

83
00:06:11.625 --> 00:06:16.166
<b>that will make us victorious,</b>
<b>or those that will make us defeated.</b>

84
00:06:16.166 --> 00:06:21.291
<b>We have to think because this</b>
<b>is our Mahabharata,</b>

85
00:06:21.291 --> 00:06:26.833
<b>and both victory and defeat in it are ours.</b>

86
00:06:26.833 --> 00:06:30.375
<b>A small example</b>

87
00:06:30.375 --> 00:06:33.833
<b>Today I have decided to be healthy.</b>

88
00:06:33.833 --> 00:06:39.416
<b>Now, having the desire to eat sweets</b>
<b>is very natural.</b>

89
00:06:39.416 --> 00:06:41.458
<b>Eating sweets</b>

90
00:06:41.458 --> 00:06:43.875
<b>this is the first decision.</b>

91
00:06:43.875 --> 00:06:46.666
<b>And if you must eat, then how much </b>

92
00:06:46.666 --> 00:06:48.416
<b>this is control.</b>

93
00:06:48.416 --> 00:06:54.875
<b>This will determine the difference between</b>
<b>a strong and a weak body.</b>

94
00:06:54.875 --> 00:07:00.625
<b>And this is the small battle</b>
<b>of the Mahabharata within us,</b>

95
00:07:00.625 --> 00:07:03.125
<b> in which we have to choose</b>

96
00:07:03.125 --> 00:07:04.875
<b>this</b>

97
00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:06.458
<b>or that.</b>

98
00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:11.375
<b>Was Dhritarashtra's love for his sons wrong? </b>

99
00:07:11.375 --> 00:07:16.791
<b>Was Dhritarashtra's love for his sons wrong? </b>

100
00:07:16.791 --> 00:07:18.250
<b>No, </b>

101
00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.125
<b>absolutely not.</b>

102
00:07:20.125 --> 00:07:21.958
<b>It was natural.</b>

103
00:07:21.958 --> 00:07:27.416
<b>What was wrong was closing the eyes</b>
<b>of the mind in that love.</b>

104
00:07:27.416 --> 00:07:32.333
<b>Earlier, out of love and affection,</b>
<b>he ignored his sons' minor mistakes. </b>

105
00:07:32.333 --> 00:07:33.791
<b>Later,</b>

106
00:07:33.791 --> 00:07:40.166
<b>Later, driven by the greed for power,</b>

107
00:07:40.166 --> 00:07:41.875
<b>he turned a blind eye</b>

108
00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:48.083
<b>many major wrongdoings and failed</b>
<b>to provide proper guidance. That was wrong.</b>

109
00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:49.541
<b>And then,</b>

110
00:07:49.541 --> 00:07:51.958
<b>it was too late.</b>

111
00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:57.166
<b>The destructive war of Mahabharata</b>
<b>arrived at the doorstep,</b>

112
00:07:57.166 --> 00:08:04.916
<b>where the very sons he loved were sacrificed.</b>

113
00:08:04.916 --> 00:08:06.791
<b>But was </b>

114
00:08:06.791 --> 00:08:10.750
<b> it really love?</b>

115
00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.458
<b>Staying silent like this,</b>

116
00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:21.041
<b>knowing that our own are taking the</b>
<b>wrong path with every step?</b>

117
00:08:21.041 --> 00:08:22.208
<b>This was </b>

118
00:08:22.208 --> 00:08:29.875
<b>false attachment and selfishness</b>
<b>disguised as love, wasn't it?</b>

119
00:08:29.875 --> 00:08:33.250
<b>Now you tell me,</b>

120
00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:36.000
<b>What is more important?</b>

121
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.541
<b>That those</b>

122
00:08:37.541 --> 00:08:42.916
<b>we love don't find our words harsh?</b>

123
00:08:42.916 --> 00:08:44.041
<b>Or that</b>

124
00:08:44.041 --> 00:08:51.375
<b>nothing terrible ever happens to them?</b>

125
00:08:51.375 --> 00:08:57.041
<b>If you truly care about someone's health,</b>
<b>and the medicine is bitter,</b>

126
00:08:57.041 --> 00:09:01.125
<b>it's still right to give it, isn't it?</b>

127
00:09:01.125 --> 00:09:06.000
<b>Letting health deteriorate for fear of bitterness</b>

128
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.708
<b>can be selfishness,</b>

129
00:09:08.708 --> 00:09:11.583
<b>blind attachment,</b>

130
00:09:11.583 --> 00:09:14.625
<b>but love? </b>

131
00:09:14.625 --> 00:09:17.500
<b>Definitely not Love.</b>

132
00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:21.000
<b>The very definition of love</b>

133
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.791
<b>is that in which the</b>
<b>other's well-being comes first.</b>

134
00:09:25.791 --> 00:09:30.750
<b>It is necessary for us to become a person</b>

135
00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:37.000
<b>who believes in being good</b>
<b>rather than just looking good.</b>

136
00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:45.875
<b>And it is equally important for us to keep such</b>
<b>loved ones around us whose words may </b>

137
00:09:45.875 --> 00:09:47.791
<b>sometimes be bitter,</b>

138
00:09:47.791 --> 00:09:50.958
<b>but whose intentions are always</b>

139
00:09:50.958 --> 00:09:52.041
<b>true  </b>

140
00:09:52.041 --> 00:09:53.958
<b>and sweet.</b>

141
00:09:54.583 --> 00:09:58.750


142
00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:04.333
<b>Dhritarashtra is just hoping in his mind</b>

143
00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:07.250
<b>that if only the Pandavas change their mind</b>

144
00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:11.250
<b>and back away from the war.</b>

145
00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.541
<b>In that case,</b>

146
00:10:13.541 --> 00:10:18.375
<b>the Kauravas will win unopposed.</b>

147
00:10:18.375 --> 00:10:20.041
<b>But </b>

148
00:10:20.041 --> 00:10:23.208
<b>there is a big fear</b>

149
00:10:23.208 --> 00:10:27.625
<b>what if the Kauravas do that?</b>

150
00:10:27.625 --> 00:10:31.166
<b>What if they back down?</b>

151
00:10:31.166 --> 00:10:33.666
<b>The fear is natural.</b>

152
00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:42.208
<b>He has sent his sons to fight a battle</b>
<b>of adharma on such a holy site.</b>

153
00:10:42.208 --> 00:10:43.333
<b>But now</b>

154
00:10:43.333 --> 00:10:45.750
<b>it's too late,</b>

155
00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:53.666
<b>and in such a situation, there is no way out</b>
<b>except hollow hopes and fear.</b>

156
00:10:53.666 --> 00:10:58.166
<b>What a misfortune it is for any leader</b>

157
00:10:58.166 --> 00:11:06.625
<b>to have doubt in the mind instead of</b>
<b>courage when the battle is ahead.</b>

158
00:11:06.625 --> 00:11:11.875
<b>In professional life, we are also leaders,</b>

159
00:11:11.875 --> 00:11:13.541
<b>whether of others </b>

160
00:11:13.541 --> 00:11:15.583
<b>or of ourselves.</b>

161
00:11:15.583 --> 00:11:19.083
<b>We too will face many battles,</b>

162
00:11:19.083 --> 00:11:24.708
<b>and our courage on the field will depend on</b>

163
00:11:24.708 --> 00:11:29.250
<b>how true our reason for fighting the battle is.</b>

164
00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>Where there is truth,</b>

165
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:35.083
<b>where is fear?</b>

166
00:11:35.083 --> 00:11:36.416
<b>And</b>

167
00:11:36.416 --> 00:11:39.333
<b>most importantly,</b>

168
00:11:39.333 --> 00:11:42.958
<b>a battle can never be won alone.</b>

169
00:11:42.958 --> 00:11:50.333
<b>We need to keep such people around</b>
<b>us who can advise us, </b>

170
00:11:50.333 --> 00:11:53.416
<b>who truly want our good,</b>

171
00:11:53.416 --> 00:11:57.583
<b>not just look good in front of us.</b>

172
00:11:57.583 --> 00:11:59.791
<b>If we find such well-wishers,</b>

173
00:11:59.791 --> 00:12:07.833
<b>it is in our interest to listen to</b>
<b>their advice without any ego.</b>

174
00:12:07.833 --> 00:12:12.208
<b>Dhritarashtra did nothing like this.</b>

175
00:12:12.208 --> 00:12:15.166
<b>Not only were the eyes of his body closed,</b>

176
00:12:15.166 --> 00:12:19.083
<b>but he also closed the eyes of his conscience.</b>

177
00:12:19.083 --> 00:12:25.166
<b>He ignored all the advice that fell on his ears.</b>

178
00:12:25.166 --> 00:12:26.833
<b>Now,</b>

179
00:12:26.833 --> 00:12:29.875
<b>the war of Mahabharata is ahead,</b>

180
00:12:29.875 --> 00:12:31.583
<b>and</b>

181
00:12:31.583 --> 00:12:35.750
<b> both fear and doubt are gnawing at him.</b>

